# Target
Run an empirical jj-colocation trial for lane `audio`. The live repo is /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/audio-shokunin on branch `main`; your sandbox is /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/.

# Change
1. **Build the sandbox.** Run `git clone --bare /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/audio-shokunin /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/remote.git`, then `git clone /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/remote.git /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane`. Overlay the live working tree's untracked and ignored files so the trial sees real content: `rsync -a --exclude=.git --exclude=.jj /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/audio-shokunin/ /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane/` (the live side is read-only). Record `git -C /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane status --porcelain | wc -l` and the 10 largest untracked or ignored files.
2. **Colocate through the helper.** Run `HYAKU_STATE=/fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/state /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/scripts/hyaku/jj-lane.sh init /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane audio`, then confirm the repo config it set. Time `jj status` over 3 runs from /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane. Record:
   - the helper's state line;
   - any init warning;
   - whether git HEAD is attached (`git symbolic-ref -q HEAD`);
   - whether `git status --porcelain` changed compared with step 1 (expected: no change; every untracked path is still `??`).
3. **Measure the default auto-track alternative.** Copy the sandbox with `cp -a /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane-autotrack`, set auto-track to "all()" there, and record:
   - how many files jj would snapshot into the working-copy commit;
   - any `new file too large` refusals;
   - the snapshot time.
4. **Simulate a round commit with the real helper.**
   - Prepare: append a line to LOG.md, create corpus/lessons/round-999-jjtrial.md, and leave one scratch file untracked.
   - Commit and push: `HYAKU_STATE=/fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/state /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/scripts/hyaku/jj-lane.sh commit /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane --as audio -m "round-999: jj trial" -- LOG.md corpus/lessons/round-999-jjtrial.md`. It must print `committed <hash>` and `pushed <hash>`.
   - Verify:
     - the author and committer identity;
     - `git log -1 --format=%H -- LOG.md` equals the pushed hash;
     - `git merge-base --is-ancestor <hash> main` succeeds;
     - `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/scripts/hyaku/jj-lane.sh state /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane` shows ahead=0;
     - the sandbox remote has the commit;
     - the scratch file is still untracked and its content is intact.
   - Then simulate an operator push: commit and push a `considerthese/` file from a second clone of the sandbox remote. Rerun a helper commit of another path and confirm it recovers by fetch + rebase.
5. **Run the lane's own git-touching checks in the sandbox.**
   - Read /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/audio-shokunin/SKILL.md (its gate/selftest registry) and the lane's tools/ or scripts/.
   - Pick up to 3 gates or selftests that invoke git. Run each against /fast/scratch/jj-wave/JjTrialAudio/lane only, never the live repo, with a 300 s timeout.
   - Record each exit code.
   - Separate failures caused by colocation (detached HEAD, index state, untracked handling) from pre-existing failures by re-running the same command in a plain git clone without jj.

# Acceptance
The report contains:
- per-step observed results, each with its command;
- a PASS/FAIL table for steps 2–5;
- the colocation hazards specific to this lane (big files, nested .git dirs, symlinks, LFS/.gitattributes, hooks, generated directories);
- the exact per-lane config or ignore additions you recommend.

Lane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.

Report: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/hyaku/jj-w1/reports/JjTrialAudio.md

